spec:
  grid: 14-19 rows x 15-19 cols
  colors: input uses only black(0), grey(5), yellow(4); output replaces some grey with red(2)
  background: random-looking binary noise of black and grey cells; grey density 40-55% of total grid
  plus_motifs:
    count: 4-7 per grid
    shape: axis-aligned plus (center + up/down/left/right), 5 cells if interior, 3-4 if center on grid edge
    composition: each plus has 2-4 yellow cells and 1-3 grey cells; yellow+grey = plus size
    yellow_connectivity: yellow cells within each plus form one 8-connected component
    uniqueness: each 8-connected yellow component maps to exactly one plus center
    non_overlap: plus motifs share no cells with each other
    separation: manhattan distance between any two plus centers >= 6
    edge_clipping: 0-1 plus centers per grid may sit on grid border (row 0/last or col 0/last) [observed]
    embedding: all plus cells (yellow and grey) sit within the grey+yellow foreground region; no black cell inside any plus
  transform: for each plus, recolor its grey cells to red; yellow and black cells unchanged

